better-Y - a mod of the stock launcher for the Innioasis Y1

Copyright (c) 2026 better-Y Team


WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS
------------------------

The MIT License below applies to what was written for this project, and to that alone:

  * our own code and resources - the com/innioasis/ipp package, IppActivity, IppQueueActivity,
    and the drawables, layouts and strings added with them
  * the build, patch and image scripts under build/, and the Java sources they compile
  * the wording of the strings, help texts and documentation in this repository


WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
----------------------

The Innioasis Y1 launcher, package com.innioasis.y1, is proprietary software of INNIOASIS. This
project modifies it; it does not replace it and does not license it. All rights in that code, and
in the firmware it ships with, belong to their respective authors.

  * stock.diff quotes lines of that launcher as the context a patch needs. Those lines are
    INNIOASIS's, are reproduced only to identify where our changes go, and no license of ours
    applies to them.

  * delete.txt names files of that launcher. Naming them is not distributing them.

  * A built APK is our code compiled into theirs. The MIT License covers our part of it wherever
    it ends up - including in a closed-source or commercial build - and says nothing about the rest.

  * The firmware images attached to releases (system.img, rom.zip) are the factory Innioasis Y1
    3.1.2 partitions - the same ones published by y1-community/y1-stock-rom - with our launcher put
    in place of the stock one. Everything in them except that one file is INNIOASIS's, distributed
    unmodified for the practical reason that a system APK cannot be installed any other way.

  * The signing key used for builds is the public AOSP platform testkey from the Android Open
    Source Project (Apache-2.0). It is not included here; the README says where to get it and what
    fingerprint to verify.

  * Third-party libraries inside the stock launcher (AndroidX, Glide, Kotlin, xCrash and others)
    carry their own licenses, held by their own authors.

No affiliation with or endorsement by INNIOASIS is claimed. "Innioasis" and "Y1" are used only to
say which device this is for.


